Dialogue: 0,0:00:12.00,0:00:14.66,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I'd been driving for\Nalmost 11 hours when the
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.66,0:00:16.50,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}detour signs pushed me off the interstate.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:17.22,0:00:20.00,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}The road narrowed to two\Nlanes, then the radio
Dialogue: 0,0:00:20.00,0:00:22.34,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}lost its station, and for a long time the
Dialogue: 0,0:00:22.34,0:00:24.14,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}only light out there\Nwas my own headlights.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.22,0:00:28.86,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}Around two in the morning, I saw a gas\Nstation sign glowing over the fields.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:29.54,0:00:34.06,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}The pumps were on, the store was dark, and\Nthere was one other car parked by the air
Dialogue: 0,0:00:34.06,0:00:36.86,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}machine with its engine\Nrunning and nobody inside.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.74,0:00:40.16,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}This was in October, about six years ago.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:40.84,0:00:45.02,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I was 24 and moving back home to Missouri\Nafter a job in Colorado fell apart.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:46.00,0:00:49.38,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}Everything I owned was in the backseat\Nof a Corolla with a cracked windshield.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:49.98,0:00:52.22,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I'd planned to stop for the\Nnight in a motel somewhere
Dialogue: 0,0:00:52.22,0:00:54.70,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}in western Kansas, but I kept telling
Dialogue: 0,0:00:54.80,0:00:57.82,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}myself one more hour, and\Nby the time the detour
Dialogue: 0,0:00:57.82,0:00:59.72,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}came up, I was too tired to be smart
Dialogue: 0,0:00:59.70,0:01:00.50,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}about it.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:00.94,0:01:03.34,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I pulled up to the pump,\Nfarthest from the other car.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:04.00,0:01:07.94,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}It was an older station wagon, dark green\Nwith wood panels on the sides and a bumper
Dialogue: 0,0:01:07.94,0:01:10.10,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}sticker that said, Proud\NParent of an Honor Student,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:10.24,0:01:11.50,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}with the name of the school scratched
Dialogue: 0,0:01:11.50,0:01:12.30,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}off.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:12.42,0:01:14.30,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}The exhaust was rising in the cold.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:14.76,0:01:16.70,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}The headlights were off,\Nbut the dome light was
Dialogue: 0,0:01:16.70,0:01:18.80,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}on, and I could see a\Njacket on the passenger
Dialogue: 0,0:01:18.80,0:01:20.76,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}seat and a fast food bag on the dashboard.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:21.78,0:01:23.78,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I figured whoever it\Nbelonged to was in the
Dialogue: 0,0:01:23.78,0:01:24.70,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}bathroom around the side of the building.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:25.58,0:01:27.00,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I filled the tank and waited.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:27.20,0:01:28.34,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I don't know why I waited.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:28.76,0:01:32.68,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I think I wanted to see someone walk back\Nto that car, just so I could stop thinking
Dialogue: 0,0:01:32.68,0:01:33.48,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}about it.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:34.14,0:01:34.94,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}Nobody came.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:35.40,0:01:37.44,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}The pump clicked off,\Nthe screen asked if I
Dialogue: 0,0:01:37.44,0:01:39.76,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}wanted a receipt, and the whole time that
Dialogue: 0,0:01:39.76,0:01:43.36,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}engine kept idling, steady, like\Nit had been running for hours.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:44.12,0:01:45.72,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I didn't go check the bathroom.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:46.08,0:01:47.70,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I got back in my car and left.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:48.60,0:01:52.42,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}About twenty minutes later, the\Ndetour signs ended at a truck stop.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:52.72,0:01:55.64,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}It was the first real building\NI'd seen in a long time.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:56.24,0:01:58.76,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}A diner on one side, a\Ncouple of semis parked
Dialogue: 0,0:01:58.76,0:02:00.94,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}out back with their running lights on, and
Dialogue: 0,0:02:00.94,0:02:04.70,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}a sign that said, Open 24 hours,\Nwith two of the letters burned out.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:05.76,0:02:07.66,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I parked near the\Nentrance because I needed
Dialogue: 0,0:02:07.66,0:02:09.88,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}coffee, and I needed to sit somewhere with
Dialogue: 0,0:02:09.88,0:02:10.74,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}people for a while.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:12.18,0:02:15.62,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}Inside, it was warm and smelled\Nlike burnt coffee and bacon grease.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:16.16,0:02:18.02,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}There was a trucker at\Nthe counter, reading
Dialogue: 0,0:02:18.02,0:02:20.46,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}his phone, an older man asleep in a booth
Dialogue: 0,0:02:20.46,0:02:21.88,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}by the window, and one waitress.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:22.80,0:02:25.48,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}Her name tag said D.\NShe looked about fifty,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:25.82,0:02:27.74,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}and she called me Honey\Nbefore I'd even sat
Dialogue: 0,0:02:27.74,0:02:28.54,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}down.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:28.90,0:02:31.68,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I took a booth facing\Nthe door, ordered coffee
Dialogue: 0,0:02:31.68,0:02:33.70,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}and a slice of pie, and started looking at
Dialogue: 0,0:02:33.70,0:02:38.04,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}the map on my phone, trying to figure\Nout how far I was from anything.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:39.76,0:02:41.46,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}That's when the couple came in.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:41.96,0:02:44.00,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}They were young, maybe my age.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:44.78,0:02:46.96,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}The guy wore a gray\Nhoodie, and the girl had
Dialogue: 0,0:02:46.96,0:02:49.12,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}on a denim jacket that\Nwas too thin for the
Dialogue: 0,0:02:49.12,0:02:49.92,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}weather.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:49.76,0:02:52.14,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}It had started to rain\Noutside, and the shoulders
Dialogue: 0,0:02:52.14,0:02:53.56,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}of their jackets were dark with it.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:54.32,0:02:57.52,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}They were arguing in that low,\Ntight way people argue in public.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:58.38,0:03:00.20,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}As they walked past my\Nbooth, the girl said,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:00.48,0:03:01.62,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}Every single time, Ray.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:01.86,0:03:02.96,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}Every single time.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:03.76,0:03:04.56,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}He didn't answer.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:05.24,0:03:07.58,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}They sat two booths down\Nfrom me, across the
Dialogue: 0,0:03:07.58,0:03:09.98,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}aisle, and D. went over with menus and two
Dialogue: 0,0:03:09.98,0:03:11.06,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}waters like it was nothing.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:11.96,0:03:13.48,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I didn't think much about it.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:14.16,0:03:14.96,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I ate my pie.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:15.54,0:03:17.90,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I heard bits of their\Nconversation, something about
Dialogue: 0,0:03:17.90,0:03:20.26,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}a wrong turn and whose idea it had been
Dialogue: 0,0:03:20.26,0:03:21.14,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}to leave so late.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:21.62,0:03:24.48,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}The girl had a laugh that\Nwasn't really a laugh.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:24.84,0:03:26.90,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}At one point, Ray said, We'll be fine.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:27.30,0:03:28.10,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}We're almost there.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:28.72,0:03:29.74,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}She didn't say anything back.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:30.62,0:03:32.64,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}After a while, I got up\Nto use the restroom.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:32.94,0:03:35.22,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}It was at the end of a short\Nhallway past the kitchen.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:35.80,0:03:37.52,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I remember the hallway\Nbecause one of the fluorescent
Dialogue: 0,0:03:37.52,0:03:39.02,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}lights was flickering, and there
Dialogue: 0,0:03:39.02,0:03:42.34,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}was a corkboard on the wall with business\Ncards and a flyer for a missing dog.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:42.86,0:03:45.06,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I was in there maybe\Nthree or four minutes.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:45.68,0:03:47.90,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I washed my hands,\Nsplashed water on my face,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:47.90,0:03:50.08,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}and looked at myself in\Nthe mirror, thinking
Dialogue: 0,0:03:50.08,0:03:51.62,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I really needed to find a bed.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:52.86,0:03:56.88,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}When I came out and walked back toward my\Nbooth, the bell over the front door rang.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:58.00,0:04:01.58,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}It was them, the same\Ncouple, gray hoodie, thin
Dialogue: 0,0:04:01.58,0:04:03.94,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}denim jacket, the\Nshoulders of both jackets
Dialogue: 0,0:04:03.94,0:04:04.74,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}dark with rain.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:05.38,0:04:07.68,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}They walked in the same\Nway, him a step ahead,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:08.08,0:04:09.72,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}her a little behind with her arms crossed,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:09.90,0:04:15.52,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}and as they passed me, the girl said,\NEvery single time, Ray, every single time.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:16.28,0:04:17.50,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I stopped in the aisle.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:18.30,0:04:20.74,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I looked over at the booth two down\Nfrom mine, where they'd been sitting.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:21.16,0:04:22.04,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}It was empty.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:22.86,0:04:25.76,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}No menus, no glasses, no\Nwet rings on the table.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:26.20,0:04:28.66,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}It had been wiped down like\Nnobody had used it all night.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:29.38,0:04:31.10,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}They sat in that same booth.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:31.94,0:04:34.44,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}Dee came over with two\Nmenus and two waters, and
Dialogue: 0,0:04:34.44,0:04:36.90,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}she smiled at them, and she said, Evening
Dialogue: 0,0:04:36.90,0:04:37.70,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}you two.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:37.78,0:04:38.62,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}Rough night out there?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:39.12,0:04:41.30,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}Exactly how you'd greet\Nsomeone who just walked in.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:42.10,0:04:45.00,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I sat down because I didn't\Nknow what else to do.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:45.78,0:04:46.74,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}My coffee was still there.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:46.80,0:04:47.76,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}My plate was still there.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:48.28,0:04:49.34,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I watched them.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:49.82,0:04:52.02,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I kept waiting for one\Nof them to look at me,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:52.08,0:04:54.26,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}or laugh, or for this to turn into some
Dialogue: 0,0:04:54.26,0:04:55.06,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}kind of joke.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:55.98,0:04:56.98,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}Ray was rubbing his eyes.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:57.54,0:04:59.68,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}The girl was looking out the\Nwindow at the parking lot.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:00.20,0:05:02.48,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}They were having the same conversation.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:03.26,0:05:04.06,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}Wrong turn.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:04.38,0:05:05.18,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}Leaving too late.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:05.24,0:05:07.08,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}And then Ray said, We'll be fine.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:07.30,0:05:08.10,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}We're almost there.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:08.60,0:05:10.32,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I looked at the trucker at the counter.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:10.82,0:05:12.88,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}He hadn't looked up from\Nhis phone the whole time.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:13.74,0:05:15.74,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}The old man in the window\Nbooth was still asleep.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:16.52,0:05:19.14,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}Nobody else in that room seemed\Nto think anything was wrong.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:19.88,0:05:22.20,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I left a twenty on the\Ntable and walked out.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:22.58,0:05:23.48,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I didn't wait for change.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:23.82,0:05:27.30,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}When I got outside, the rain had\Nstopped, and the parking lot was dry.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:27.70,0:05:28.50,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}Completely dry.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:29.08,0:05:29.88,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}No puddles.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:30.08,0:05:31.12,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}Nothing wet on my windshield.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:32.48,0:05:34.44,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I stood there for a second,\Nlooking at the ground.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:34.92,0:05:37.24,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}Then I got in my car,\Nlocked the doors, and sat
Dialogue: 0,0:05:37.24,0:05:39.14,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}with the engine running for a long time.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:40.68,0:05:43.00,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I didn't want to drive past\Nthat gas station again.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:43.72,0:05:45.28,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I didn't want to go back inside, either.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:45.46,0:05:48.26,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}So I just sat there\Nuntil the sky started to
Dialogue: 0,0:05:48.26,0:05:50.26,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}turn gray, and then I followed the signs
Dialogue: 0,0:05:50.26,0:05:51.06,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}back to the interstate.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:51.76,0:05:54.40,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I didn't pass the gas\Nstation on the way back.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:54.94,0:05:56.14,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I took the same road.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:56.18,0:05:56.98,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I'm sure of that.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:57.58,0:05:58.50,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}It just wasn't there.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:59.38,0:06:02.34,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I had a dash cam back then,\None of those cheap ones
Dialogue: 0,0:06:02.34,0:06:04.16,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}that records over itself every few hours.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:05.06,0:06:07.56,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}When I finally got home\Nand checked it, most
Dialogue: 0,0:06:07.56,0:06:08.86,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}of that night had\Nalready been overwritten.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:09.68,0:06:12.44,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}The only file left starts\Nas I pull into the truck
Dialogue: 0,0:06:12.44,0:06:14.42,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}stop parking lot at 2.14 in the morning.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:15.32,0:06:18.00,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I park, the camera keeps\Nrecording, and about
Dialogue: 0,0:06:18.00,0:06:20.22,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}a minute later, the dark\Ngreen station wagon
Dialogue: 0,0:06:20.22,0:06:22.16,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}pulls into the spot right in front of me.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:22.36,0:06:25.50,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}Engine running, dome\Nlight on, nobody inside.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:26.52,0:06:29.22,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}The date on that clip is October 14th.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:29.58,0:06:32.10,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}The year is the one before\NI ever drove that road.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:32.78,0:06:35.62,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I still drive that interstate\Na couple of times a year.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:36.38,0:06:38.66,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}If the detour signs are\Nup, I don't take them.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:39.28,0:06:41.70,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I find the last town\Nbefore the exit, I park
Dialogue: 0,0:06:41.70,0:06:43.96,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}somewhere well lit, and I sleep in my car
Dialogue: 0,0:06:43.96,0:06:44.76,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}until morning.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:52.71,0:06:55.03,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I ran out of gas on a\Nstate highway in Nevada
Dialogue: 0,0:06:55.03,0:06:57.87,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}a little after 10 at night, about 40 miles
Dialogue: 0,0:06:57.87,0:06:58.67,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}from the nearest town.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:59.35,0:07:00.31,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}That part was my fault.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:00.59,0:07:03.47,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I was 22, driving from\NReno to see my sister in
Dialogue: 0,0:07:03.47,0:07:05.31,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}Arizona, and I'd skipped the last station
Dialogue: 0,0:07:05.31,0:07:08.53,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}because the prices were ridiculous and\NI was sure there'd be another one soon.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:08.99,0:07:09.79,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}There wasn't.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:10.41,0:07:13.91,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}The car started sputtering\Non a long straight stretch
Dialogue: 0,0:07:13.91,0:07:16.23,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}with nothing on either side but sagebrush
Dialogue: 0,0:07:16.23,0:07:17.05,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}and dark hills.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:17.05,0:07:20.27,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I coasted onto the shoulder\Nand sat there with
Dialogue: 0,0:07:20.27,0:07:22.47,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}my hazards on, listening to the engine
Dialogue: 0,0:07:22.47,0:07:23.57,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}tick as it cooled.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:24.19,0:07:25.87,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I had one bar of signal.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:26.51,0:07:28.91,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I called roadside\Nassistance, gave them the
Dialogue: 0,0:07:28.91,0:07:31.29,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}mile marker from my map app, and the woman
Dialogue: 0,0:07:31.29,0:07:34.05,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}on the phone told me a tow truck\Nwould be there in about 90 minutes.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:35.07,0:07:36.25,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}She asked if I felt safe.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:36.75,0:07:39.63,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I said, yes, because what\Nelse are you supposed to say?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:40.37,0:07:43.35,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}The first thing I noticed\Nwas how quiet it was.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:43.35,0:07:46.53,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}When the engine stopped\Nticking, there was nothing.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:47.35,0:07:49.97,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}No wind, no insects, no traffic.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:50.29,0:07:51.87,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I could hear my own breathing.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:52.93,0:07:54.73,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}Every few minutes, I'd\Nturn the key just far
Dialogue: 0,0:07:54.73,0:07:56.25,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}enough to check the time on the dashboard,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:56.63,0:07:58.33,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}then turned it off again\Nto save the battery.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:58.69,0:08:03.63,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I had half a bottle of water and a bag of\Nsunflower seeds, and I remember rationing
Dialogue: 0,0:08:03.63,0:08:06.81,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}the water like I was in a survival\Nmovie, which is funny now.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:07.73,0:08:10.83,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}About thirty minutes in,\Nheadlights came up behind me.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:10.83,0:08:14.07,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}My stomach dropped, but then I\Nsaw the light bar on the roof.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:14.35,0:08:15.57,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}It was a sheriff's deputy.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:16.09,0:08:18.47,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}He pulled in behind me and\Nwalked up with a flashlight,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:18.55,0:08:20.79,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}an older guy with a gray mustache
Dialogue: 0,0:08:20.79,0:08:22.25,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}and a tired, friendly face.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:22.87,0:08:23.81,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I explained what happened.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:24.53,0:08:26.05,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}He shook his head and\Nlaughed a little, not
Dialogue: 0,0:08:26.05,0:08:28.21,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}in a mean way, and said I wasn't the first
Dialogue: 0,0:08:28.35,0:08:29.51,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}and wouldn't be the last.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:30.27,0:08:33.27,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}He went back to his car and came\Nback with two bottles of water.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:33.69,0:08:37.13,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}Then he leaned down to my window,\Nand his voice changed a little.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:37.13,0:08:40.91,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}He said, listen, keep your doors\Nlocked until the tow gets here.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:41.33,0:08:43.49,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}If anybody walks up to\Nthe car, you don't roll
Dialogue: 0,0:08:43.49,0:08:45.81,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}the window down, you call 911, and you
Dialogue: 0,0:08:45.81,0:08:47.09,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}tell them Deputy Harlan is out here.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:47.97,0:08:50.41,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I asked him if something\Nhad happened out here.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:51.15,0:08:53.57,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}He looked down the road for\Na second, then back at me.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:54.11,0:08:57.21,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}He said, people walk this\Nroad at night sometimes.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:57.85,0:08:59.05,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I don't stop for them anymore.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:59.89,0:09:03.41,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}Then he told me to have a good night,\Ngot back in his cruiser, and pulled away.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:04.19,0:09:07.35,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I watched his taillights\Nfor a long time until they
Dialogue: 0,0:09:07.35,0:09:09.97,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}turned into one red dot and then nothing.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:11.13,0:09:13.65,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}After that, the quiet felt different.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:14.57,0:09:16.77,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I locked the doors and checked them twice.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:17.25,0:09:20.25,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I sat with my phone in my lap and\Nkept looking in the side mirrors.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:20.73,0:09:23.59,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}The road behind me was a straight\Nblack line under the stars.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:23.81,0:09:27.83,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I could see maybe a quarter mile back,\Nand then it disappeared into the dark.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:28.61,0:09:31.13,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I told myself the deputy\Nwas just being careful,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:31.15,0:09:32.79,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}and he probably said that to everyone.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:33.77,0:09:36.35,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I tried playing a podcast,\Nbut I turned it off
Dialogue: 0,0:09:36.35,0:09:38.21,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}after a minute because I didn't like not
Dialogue: 0,0:09:38.21,0:09:39.01,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}being able to hear.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:39.79,0:09:43.05,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}The tow truck showed up about\Nan hour after the deputy left.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:43.53,0:09:45.55,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I almost cried when I\Nsaw the amber lights.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:46.15,0:09:49.77,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}The driver backed up in front of my\Ncar, got out, and gave me a wave.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:50.19,0:09:53.65,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}He was a big guy in a reflective\Nvest, probably in his fifties.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:54.01,0:09:54.85,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}His name was Manny.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:55.79,0:09:57.65,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}He told me to stay in the\Ncar while he hooked it up.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:57.65,0:09:58.75,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}It would only take a few minutes.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:59.19,0:10:00.77,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I nodded and stayed put.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:01.39,0:10:04.07,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I was watching him in\Nmy headlights, crouched
Dialogue: 0,0:10:04.07,0:10:06.25,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}down at the front of my car, working with
Dialogue: 0,0:10:06.25,0:10:07.05,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}the chains.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:07.31,0:10:09.83,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}And then I looked in my rearview mirror.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:10.85,0:10:13.31,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}There was a woman standing behind my car.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:14.25,0:10:15.61,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}She wasn't on the road.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:16.13,0:10:19.37,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}She was on the shoulder,\Nmaybe ten feet back, at
Dialogue: 0,0:10:19.37,0:10:21.37,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}the edge of the red glow\Nfrom my taillights.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:21.95,0:10:27.91,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}She was older, maybe sixties, thin, with\Nlong gray hair and a hiking backpack.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:28.75,0:10:31.01,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}She wasn't wearing a coat,\Nand it was cold enough
Dialogue: 0,0:10:31.01,0:10:32.57,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}that I had the heat on until the battery
Dialogue: 0,0:10:32.57,0:10:33.37,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}scared me.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:33.79,0:10:35.29,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I hadn't seen any headlights.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:35.87,0:10:37.49,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I hadn't heard footsteps on the gravel.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:38.11,0:10:39.49,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}She was just there.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:40.09,0:10:41.17,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I didn't move.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:41.57,0:10:42.85,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I watched her in the mirror.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:43.55,0:10:46.05,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}She walked up along the\Npassenger side of the
Dialogue: 0,0:10:46.05,0:10:48.25,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}car, slowly, and stopped at the back door.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:49.09,0:10:51.85,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}Then she reached out\Nand pulled the handle.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:53.05,0:10:53.85,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}It was locked.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:54.31,0:10:57.33,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}She pulled it again, harder, and\Nthe whole car rocked a little.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:57.85,0:11:00.03,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}Then she bent down and looked\Nthrough the back window.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:00.85,0:11:01.91,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}She wasn't looking at me.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:02.15,0:11:05.55,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}She was looking at the back seat, like\Nshe expected someone to be sitting there.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:06.37,0:11:07.37,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I hit the horn.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:08.07,0:11:08.87,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I don't know why.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:09.13,0:11:10.83,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}It was the only thing I could think of.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:11.79,0:11:13.03,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}Manny stood up in front of the car.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:13.55,0:11:16.05,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}The woman straightened up\Nand walked to my window,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:16.37,0:11:18.17,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}the passenger side, and knocked on
Dialogue: 0,0:11:18.17,0:11:20.51,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}the glass with one knuckle, very politely.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:21.69,0:11:23.25,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}She leaned down and said,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:23.49,0:11:24.51,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}My car's just up the road.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:24.75,0:11:25.55,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I've got a flat.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:25.59,0:11:27.11,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I just need a ride to it.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:27.61,0:11:29.25,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}Her voice was normal.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:29.91,0:11:31.35,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}That's what I keep coming back to.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:31.75,0:11:36.71,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}It was a completely normal voice, a little\Nhoarse, like somebody's grandmother.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:37.63,0:11:38.51,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I shook my head.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:39.45,0:11:40.55,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}She smiled at me and said,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:40.99,0:11:45.07,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}It's right up there and pointed down the\Nhighway, in the direction I'd been driving.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:46.67,0:11:48.85,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}Manny was walking around the\Nfront of my car now, saying,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:48.95,0:11:50.11,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}Hey, hey, ma'am.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:50.67,0:11:52.45,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I looked at him for maybe a second.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:52.97,0:11:55.01,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}When I looked back at the\Nwindow, she wasn't there.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:55.95,0:11:57.83,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I turned all the way around in my seat.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:58.25,0:11:59.15,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}The shoulder was empty.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:59.39,0:12:00.23,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}The road was empty.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:01.09,0:12:03.13,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}Manny walked all the way around\Nmy car with his flashlight.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:03.55,0:12:05.91,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}He walked back along the\Nshoulder maybe fifty yards.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:05.91,0:12:08.07,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}There was nothing out there.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:08.67,0:12:09.71,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}No footprints that we could see.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:10.17,0:12:10.97,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}No sound.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:11.05,0:12:11.85,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}Nothing.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:11.83,0:12:13.39,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}The desert was flat for miles.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:13.75,0:12:15.45,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}There wasn't anywhere for a person to go.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:16.45,0:12:18.81,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}He came back to my window\Nand asked if I was okay.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:19.33,0:12:23.19,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I told him what she'd said, that her\Ncar was just up the road with a flat.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:24.29,0:12:25.61,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}He didn't say anything for a second.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:26.29,0:12:28.45,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}Then he asked me to ride\Nup in the truck with him.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:28.95,0:12:30.93,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}And he didn't really make\Nit sound like a question.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:31.83,0:12:34.61,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}We drove for about twenty minutes\Nbefore either of us talked.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:35.31,0:12:36.61,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}We passed the place where she'd pointed.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:37.13,0:12:38.83,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}We passed the next five miles after that.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:39.39,0:12:41.01,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}There was no car on the side of that road.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:41.53,0:12:42.33,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}There was nothing.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:43.23,0:12:44.27,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}Finally, Manny said,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:44.63,0:12:45.97,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}Did she tell you it was a flat?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:46.49,0:12:47.37,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I said yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:47.75,0:12:49.71,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}He nodded and kept his eyes on the road.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:50.29,0:12:51.09,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}He said,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:50.87,0:12:53.03,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}You're the third one this\Nyear, she's told that to.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:53.57,0:12:54.87,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}The other two opened the door.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:55.73,0:12:56.99,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I asked him what happened to them.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:57.45,0:12:58.47,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}He didn't answer me.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:58.47,0:12:59.83,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}He just turned the radio on.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:08.10,0:13:10.51,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}The summer after my\Nfreshman year of college, I
Dialogue: 0,0:13:10.51,0:13:12.56,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}drove home alone from\NDenver to Indianapolis.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:13.22,0:13:16.82,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}It's about 16 hours, and I'd convinced my\Nparents I could do it in one day if I left
Dialogue: 0,0:13:16.82,0:13:19.63,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}early enough. My dad\Nmade me promise to text
Dialogue: 0,0:13:19.63,0:13:21.74,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}him every time I stopped\Nfor gas. I thought
Dialogue: 0,0:13:21.86,0:13:24.56,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}he was being dramatic.\NThat was 19, and I'd
Dialogue: 0,0:13:24.56,0:13:26.27,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}never had anything bad happen to me, which
Dialogue: 0,0:13:26.27,0:13:28.36,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I think is the only reason\Nanybody is ever that confident.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:30.01,0:13:32.65,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I left at five in the\Nmorning. Everything went
Dialogue: 0,0:13:32.65,0:13:34.94,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}fine through eastern Colorado and most
Dialogue: 0,0:13:34.94,0:13:37.74,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}of Kansas. I listened\Nto an entire audiobook.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:38.62,0:13:40.80,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I stopped for gas outside of Salina around
Dialogue: 0,0:13:40.80,0:13:43.08,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}six in the evening, texted\Nmy dad a picture of
Dialogue: 0,0:13:43.08,0:13:45.32,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}the pump like I'd\Npromised, bought a coffee
Dialogue: 0,0:13:45.32,0:13:47.54,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}and a bag of beef jerky,\Nand got back on I-70.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:48.54,0:13:50.96,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}By the time it got dark,\NI was somewhere in eastern
Dialogue: 0,0:13:50.96,0:13:52.92,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}Kansas, and the traffic had thinned
Dialogue: 0,0:13:52.92,0:13:55.98,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}out to almost nothing. Just\Nme and the occasional semi.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:57.34,0:14:00.63,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}That's when I noticed\Nthe headlights. They were
Dialogue: 0,0:14:00.63,0:14:03.15,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}behind me. Not close. Maybe a few hundred
Dialogue: 0,0:14:03.15,0:14:06.20,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}feet back. At first I\Ndidn't think about it,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:06.20,0:14:08.08,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}but I was driving a little under the limit
Dialogue: 0,0:14:08.08,0:14:10.22,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}because I was tired, and\Nnormally people would
Dialogue: 0,0:14:10.22,0:14:13.80,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}pass me. These didn't. When I slowed down,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:14.06,0:14:16.34,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}they slowed down. When\NI sped up to see what
Dialogue: 0,0:14:16.34,0:14:19.13,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}happened, they sped up, and kept the exact
Dialogue: 0,0:14:19.13,0:14:22.48,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}same distance, like they were\Nattached to my car on a string.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:23.38,0:14:29.50,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I changed lanes. A few seconds later, so\Ndid they. I changed back. So did they.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:30.13,0:14:33.34,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I told myself it was a\Ncoincidence, that somebody
Dialogue: 0,0:14:33.34,0:14:35.74,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}else was just tired and\Nfollowing my taillights,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:35.94,0:14:39.60,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}which people do. But it\Nkept going. Twenty minutes.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:40.20,0:14:43.13,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}Forty minutes. An hour. Every time
Dialogue: 0,0:14:43.13,0:14:45.28,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I checked the mirror, they\Nwere in the same spot.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:45.96,0:14:48.18,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}Two round headlights, a little dimmer
Dialogue: 0,0:14:48.18,0:14:48.98,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}on the left side.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:49.51,0:14:52.44,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I called my dad. I\Ntried to sound calm, but
Dialogue: 0,0:14:52.44,0:14:59.48,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I don't think I did. He told me not to get
Dialogue: 0,0:14:59.48,0:15:02.18,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}right up front. I opened\Nmy map, and there was
Dialogue: 0,0:15:02.18,0:15:03.58,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}a truck stop about twelve miles ahead.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:04.51,0:15:06.10,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}He stayed on the phone\Nwith me the whole way.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:06.80,0:15:08.46,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}Every few minutes he asked, are they still
Dialogue: 0,0:15:08.46,0:15:10.30,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}there? And every time I said yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:11.13,0:15:14.65,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}The truck stop was huge.\NRows of semis in the
Dialogue: 0,0:15:14.65,0:15:16.98,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}back. A restaurant. A convenience store.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:17.75,0:15:20.48,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}Bright white lights over\Neverything. I pulled into
Dialogue: 0,0:15:20.48,0:15:22.74,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}a spot right in front of the store, close
Dialogue: 0,0:15:22.74,0:15:26.00,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}enough that I could see the cashier\Nthrough the window. I watched my mirror.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:26.70,0:15:31.68,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}The car pulled in a few seconds later. It\Ndrove slowly past the front of the store,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:32.34,0:15:34.88,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}past me, and all the way\Nto the far end of the
Dialogue: 0,0:15:34.88,0:15:36.60,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}lot, where the lights didn't reach very
Dialogue: 0,0:15:36.25,0:15:40.96,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}well. It parked facing my direction.\NThen its headlights turned off.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:42.36,0:15:43.54,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}Nobody got out.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:44.25,0:15:47.25,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I sat there for ten\Nminutes with my dad on the
Dialogue: 0,0:15:47.25,0:15:49.82,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}phone. The car didn't move. I couldn't
Dialogue: 0,0:15:49.82,0:15:52.82,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}see what kind of car it\Nwas. Just a dark shape.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:53.15,0:15:55.94,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}Maybe a sedan? I couldn't\Nsee anyone inside
Dialogue: 0,0:15:55.94,0:15:58.72,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}it. My dad said to go\Ninside and tell someone,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:58.89,0:16:00.82,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}so I did. I almost ran into the store.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:01.84,0:16:04.75,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}The cashier was a teenage\Nkid who didn't really know
Dialogue: 0,0:16:04.75,0:16:07.04,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}what to do with me.\NBut there was a trucker
Dialogue: 0,0:16:07.04,0:16:09.48,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}at the coffee station\Nwho'd heard me. An older
Dialogue: 0,0:16:09.48,0:16:11.89,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}man in a Carhartt jacket\Nwith a white beard
Dialogue: 0,0:16:11.89,0:16:14.50,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}and reading glasses\Npushed up on his head. He
Dialogue: 0,0:16:14.50,0:16:16.84,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}asked me which car. I\Npointed it out through
Dialogue: 0,0:16:16.84,0:16:19.54,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}the window. He looked\Nat it for a long time.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:20.08,0:16:22.68,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}Then he said, okay, where are you headed?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:23.56,0:16:28.22,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}His name was Walt. He told me he was going\Neast anyway, and he'd follow right behind
Dialogue: 0,0:16:28.22,0:16:30.86,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}me to the next big town,\Nabout forty miles. He
Dialogue: 0,0:16:30.86,0:16:32.62,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}said if that car tried anything, it would
Dialogue: 0,0:16:32.62,0:16:34.63,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}have to deal with eighty\Nthousand pounds of truck
Dialogue: 0,0:16:34.63,0:16:36.98,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}first. He gave me his CB channel, but
Dialogue: 0,0:16:36.98,0:16:39.44,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I didn't have a CB, so\Nwe just traded phone
Dialogue: 0,0:16:39.44,0:16:41.30,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}numbers. My dad talked to him on my phone
Dialogue: 0,0:16:41.30,0:16:43.56,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}for a minute. I don't\Nknow what they said, but
Dialogue: 0,0:16:43.56,0:16:45.62,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}after that, my dad sounded a lot calmer.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:46.38,0:16:49.68,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}We pulled out together.\NMy car, then Walt's
Dialogue: 0,0:16:49.68,0:16:52.91,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}truck, then nothing. I watched the far end
Dialogue: 0,0:16:52.91,0:16:55.41,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}of the lot as we passed,\Nand the dark car was
Dialogue: 0,0:16:55.41,0:16:57.18,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}still sitting there with its lights off.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:58.12,0:17:01.08,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}About five miles down the\Nhighway, the headlights
Dialogue: 0,0:17:01.08,0:17:04.67,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}came back. They came up\Nfast this time, much
Dialogue: 0,0:17:04.67,0:17:07.28,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}faster than before. I saw\Nthem grow in my mirror
Dialogue: 0,0:17:07.28,0:17:09.74,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}past Walt's truck, and I felt my whole
Dialogue: 0,0:17:09.74,0:17:13.63,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}body go cold. Then Walt\Nmoved. He swung his truck
Dialogue: 0,0:17:13.63,0:17:15.13,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}into the left lane, right next to the
Dialogue: 0,0:17:15.13,0:17:19.62,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}car, and stayed there, matching its speed.\NEvery time I tried to get around him, he
Dialogue: 0,0:17:19.62,0:17:24.65,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}drifted over and blocked it. He called me\Nand said, very calmly, just keep driving,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:24.78,0:17:29.58,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}sweetheart. Don't speed. I've got him. It\Nwent on for maybe two or three minutes.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:29.99,0:17:32.93,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}Then the car braked\Nhard, dropped back, and
Dialogue: 0,0:17:32.93,0:17:35.80,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}took the next exit. Walt stayed behind me
Dialogue: 0,0:17:35.80,0:17:38.17,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}for the next forty miles.\NHe followed me into
Dialogue: 0,0:17:38.17,0:17:39.80,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}the parking lot of a police station in the
Dialogue: 0,0:17:39.80,0:17:43.17,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}next town, waited while\NI went in, and then he
Dialogue: 0,0:17:43.17,0:17:44.82,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}flashed his lights twice and pulled back
Dialogue: 0,0:17:44.82,0:17:48.91,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}onto the highway. I never saw him\Nagain. I wish I'd gotten his last name.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:49.56,0:17:52.52,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I told the officer at\Nthe desk everything. I
Dialogue: 0,0:17:52.52,0:17:54.12,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}didn't have a plate number, and I didn't
Dialogue: 0,0:17:54.12,0:17:56.49,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}really expect anything\Nto come of it. He took
Dialogue: 0,0:17:56.49,0:17:59.26,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}my information, gave me a coffee, and let
Dialogue: 0,0:17:59.26,0:18:01.15,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}me sit in the lobby until\NI felt okay to drive the
Dialogue: 0,0:18:01.15,0:18:03.62,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}last few hours home.\NMy dad met me halfway.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:04.89,0:18:07.41,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}Two days later, a detective\Nfrom Kansas called
Dialogue: 0,0:18:07.41,0:18:10.45,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}me. He said a patrol car had found a dark
Dialogue: 0,0:18:10.45,0:18:12.88,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}gray sedan abandoned at\Nthat same truck stop
Dialogue: 0,0:18:12.88,0:18:14.95,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}the next morning, parked at the far end of
Dialogue: 0,0:18:14.95,0:18:18.56,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}the lot. The car had been\Nreported stolen four
Dialogue: 0,0:18:18.56,0:18:20.32,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}days earlier from a woman in Colorado.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:20.91,0:18:25.65,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}The woman had also been reported missing.\NHe asked me a lot of questions about what
Dialogue: 0,0:18:25.65,0:18:31.24,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}I saw, and I didn't have many answers. Then\Nhe asked me if I'd bought gas in Salina
Dialogue: 0,0:18:31.24,0:18:34.60,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}that evening. I said\Nyes. I'd texted my dad
Dialogue: 0,0:18:34.60,0:18:36.36,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}a picture of the pump, so I even knew the
Dialogue: 0,0:18:36.60,0:18:41.45,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}exact time. He said they'd found a receipt\Non the passenger seat of that car. It was
Dialogue: 0,0:18:41.45,0:18:43.63,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}from the same gas station\Nin Salina, Pump 4,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:43.63,0:18:47.12,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}the pump next to mine. It was printed one
Dialogue: 0,0:18:47.60,0:18:48.67,L,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}minute after my receipt.
